  "answer": "Fixed `normalizeText` in `normalize.mjs`.\n\n**Change made:** Added `.replace(/\\s+/g, ' ')` between `.trim()` and `.toLowerCase()`.\n\n**How it satisfies the spec:**\n- **Leading/trailing whitespace removed** — `String.prototype.trim()` strips JS whitespace (spaces, tabs, line breaks) from both ends.\n- **Internal whitespace runs collapsed** — `/\\s+/g` matches every nonempty run of JS whitespace and replaces it with a single ASCII space. Since `trim()` runs first, no leading/trailing space is introduced.\n- **Lowercasing** — `.toLowerCase()` is applied last, using `String.prototype.toLowerCase()`.\n- **Empty / whitespace-only input** — `trim()` yields `''`, the regex finds no matches, and `''.toLowerCase()` returns `''`.\n- **Non-string input** — the existing `typeof value !== 'string'` guard still throws a `TypeError`.\n\nThe named export (`normalizeText`) and the public tests are unchanged.",
